(NEWID(), NEWID(), @kennelId, '2025-08-31T11:00:00+00:00', NULL, 1, 1, 0, NULL, 1, 0, N'Run 1067 - Redford - Linch Rd Car Park', N'With the weather forecast promising rain at some stage today we were surprised that our numbers were increased by Haslemere Hash and others, as this area is in the south of their kingdom, to a sizeable crowd.
 We were called to circle by the J.M’s and given the normal history lesson about yellow liberals in King Henry 8th’s time having pots of paint left over and painting the Cowdray estate yellow.
 Warnings were given by the hares about them getting lost, and hoped to see us again sometime. So worried, were they, that a list of names were taken that would be consulted at regroups along the way.
 Spiderman came up with the phrase of the day "I’m taking the walkers but don’t follow me!"
 The trail started southwest, gently downhill through a couple of checks before we couldn’t go any lower, so we thought. Turning north through the first of the shiggy we reached a check where we almost lost a pack of the Haslemere crew who were running around in circles amongst the tall bracken. They needn’t have worried as ahead of us was the first of the fishhooks that caught 7 of us.
 Although a check was not found at the T-junction that followed, the trail was found going up hill to the right past Bowle House. Carrying on around our clockwise route and back into the forest, the pack was split in all directions, whilst Popeye and Chilly Willy were contemplating a fungus growing out of a decaying log. With the help of an app on their phones is was recognised as a Birch Poly Pore fungus, which is good for healing wounds. With the delay of the fungus the pack had to wait for the stragglers to catch up at the next regroup.
 With another roll call the pack proceeded across Linch Road whilst Chilly Willy still having time to sample the blackberries and carelessly pricking her finger.
 Utter confusion at the next check as two options were being called On. Dr. Blood confessed that it was nothing to do with him and blamed his co-conspirators for laying two trails back to the chariots. Popeye, Tali and Sausage Lottery were convinced that they were on the correct trail and the majority of the pack agreed leaving 3 others to find their own way back.
 With time getting on, the hash slowed down to a steady walk over the road at the Redford Road sign and wandered back in after 1hr. 15mins. The remaining hashers turning up after another 5mins.
 The normal, and well deserved, down-downs were awarded to the hares, Superman for being late, Whippet and Bika for some obscure reason. There could only be one contender for the hashit and that was Dr. Blood for so many reasons including stopping abruptly and causing a Sausage Lottery sandwich.
 A great hash was completed with a visit to The Hamilton Arms.

 Spiderman''s 2 tracks ... AND ... 
 photos by Old Faithful

